  "paper_id": "asplos-2024-maxk-gnn-extremely-fast-gpu-kernel-design-for-accelerati-4a21b743",
  "title": "MaxK-GNN: Extremely Fast GPU Kernel Design for Accelerating Graph Neural Networks Training",
  "abstract": "In the acceleration of deep neural network training, the graphics processing unit (GPU) has become the mainstream platform. GPUs face substantial challenges on Graph Neural Networks (GNNs), such as workload imbalance and memory access irregularities, leading to underutilized hardware. Existing solutions such as PyG, DGL with cuSPARSE, and GNNAdvisor frameworks partially address these challenges. However, the memory traffic involved with Sparse-Dense Matrix Matrix Multiplication (SpMM) is still significant.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-asplos-2024-4a21b743",
